def notice(slug,svc,title,short,desc,h1,lede,answer,cards,secs,faqs,related,links):
    secs=secs+[('official','Official links',linkrows(links))]
    PAGES.append(P(slug=slug,svc=svc,crumb=('Guides','/guides/'),navrel=NAV,title=title,short=short,desc=desc,h1=h1,lede=lede,answer=answer,cards=cards,sections=secs,faqs=faqs,related=related))
notice('you-cant-request-another-review-instagram-facebook','ig','“You Can’t Request Another Review”: Instagram & Facebook (2026)','You can’t request another review',
 'Instagram or Facebook says “You can’t request another review of this decision”? What it means, what is still possible, and what not to do. Paid help: $800 Instagram, $900 Facebook.',
 '“You can’t request another review of this decision.”','What that line means after a rejected appeal, and what is still possible.',
 '<strong>This line means Meta’s own appeal for that decision is finished: the in-app review button will not come back.</strong> It does not always mean the end. Check Account Status for any remaining option, keep the account untouched, and, in the EU, an out-of-court dispute body can still look at the decision. If the account was hacked first, the hacked-account route is separate. Unbanz takes these cases at a fixed fee (Instagram $800, Facebook $900), paid upfront with a 100% refund if it fails.',
 [('Appeal used','The in-app button is gone.'),('Not always final','Other routes can exist.'),('No new accounts','They get linked and disabled.')],
 [('meaning','What Meta is telling you',ul(['Your appeal was reviewed and rejected.','Meta will not offer another review of that same decision in the app.','Usually the account is now permanently disabled.'])),
  ('still','What can still be possible',ul(['A hacked account: the '+a('https://www.instagram.com/hacked/','hacked route')+' is separate from the policy appeal.','EU users: Digital Services Act dispute bodies after Meta’s appeal. See '+a('/dsa-appeal-right-instagram-facebook/','DSA rights')+'.','Linked Facebook profile disabled too: check whether it has its own appeal. See '+a('/facebook-and-instagram-disabled-together-linked-accounts/','linked accounts')+'.','Professional help that works through Meta’s processes.'])),
  ('dont','What not to do',ul(['Do not open new accounts on the same phone.','Do not pay anyone claiming to be a Meta employee.','Do not send your password or codes to anyone.']))],
 [('Does “can’t request another review” mean permanent?','Usually the account is permanently disabled, but some cases are still reversed through other routes.'),('Can I appeal again from another device?','No. The decision is tied to the account, not the device.')],
 [('/can-a-permanently-disabled-instagram-account-come-back/','Can a permanently disabled Instagram come back?'),('/instagram-appeal-rejected-what-to-check-next/','Appeal rejected')],IGL+FBL+[ACE])
notice('facebook-disabled-child-sexual-exploitation-policy','fb','Facebook Disabled for “Child Sexual Exploitation” by Mistake: What to Do (2026)','Facebook CSE policy disable',
 'Facebook or Instagram disabled your account under the Child Sexual Exploitation, Abuse and Nudity policy and you did nothing wrong? How these flags happen and how to respond.',
 'Disabled under the child sexual exploitation policy by mistake.','A serious label that is still applied in error, often to linked accounts.',
 '<strong>Appeal from the notice and keep it factual: say plainly that the account never contained or shared any such material, say what you use it for, and mention content that might have been misread.</strong> These disables are often automated and often hit linked Instagram and Facebook accounts together. Do not delete content or create new accounts. If the appeal is rejected with “You can’t request another review”, Unbanz takes Facebook cases at $900 and Instagram at $800, paid upfront with a 100% refund if it fails.',
 [('Stay factual','Short and calm.'),('Linked accounts','Often disabled together.'),('Do not delete','Leave the account as it is.')],
 [('how','How these flags happen',ul(['Automated detection misreading adult content, such as dance, fitness or swimwear videos.','Family photos of children, or medical images.','Messages or groups the account was added to without your knowledge.','A hacked account used by someone else.'])),
  ('write','What to write',ol(['Who you are and what the account is for.','That the account has never contained or shared sexual material involving minors.','Content you think was misread.','If you were hacked, when and how you noticed.','A request for a human review.'])),
  ('linked','When Instagram and Facebook both go down','<p>A disable under this policy often spreads through Accounts Center to linked accounts. Appeal each account that shows its own notice. See '+a('/facebook-and-instagram-disabled-together-linked-accounts/','disabled together')+'.</p>')],
 [('Can a CSE disable be reversed?','Sometimes, when it was a mistake. Meta decides.'),('Should I delete posts first?','No. Deleting can look like hiding evidence and changes nothing in the review.')],
 [('/instagram-disabled-child-safety-policy-flag-mistake/','Instagram child safety flag'),('/you-cant-request-another-review-instagram-facebook/','Can’t request another review')],FBL+IGL+[CS,ACE])
notice('facebook-disabled-account-integrity-notice','fb','Facebook Disabled for “Account Integrity”: What It Means (2026)','Facebook account integrity',
 'Facebook says your account doesn’t follow the Community Standards on account integrity? What triggers it, how to appeal and what to do if the appeal fails. Paid help $900.',
 'Facebook disabled for account integrity.','What the account integrity label covers and how to answer it.',
 '<strong>“Account integrity” is Meta’s label for things like fake or duplicate accounts, impersonation, suspicious logins, buying or selling accounts and accounts linked to others that broke the rules.</strong> Appeal from the notice within the window Meta shows, confirm your identity if asked, and explain who you are and how you use the account. Do not make a new profile: new accounts are often disabled under the same label within hours. If the appeal fails, Unbanz takes Facebook cases for $900, paid upfront with a 100% refund if it fails.',
 [('Broad label','Covers many triggers.'),('Identity check','Use the official upload only.'),('No new profile','It gets disabled too.')],
 [('triggers','Common triggers',ul(['A name that does not match your ID.','Several profiles for one person.','Logins from new countries, VPNs or shared devices.','Being linked to an account that was disabled.','A hacker’s activity on your profile.'])),
  ('new-account','Why the new account was disabled immediately','<p>People often make a new profile with a new email and real details, and see it disabled within hours under the same label. Meta connects new accounts to the disabled one through device, phone, network and Accounts Center. See '+a('/new-account-disabled-immediately-account-integrity/','new account disabled immediately')+'.</p>'),
  ('write','What to write',ol(['Your real name, as on your ID.','That this is your only profile, or why there were two.','Any hack or unusual login you noticed.','A request for a human review.']))],
 [('Is account integrity the same as being hacked?','No, but a hack can cause it.'),('How long does the appeal take?','Often days, sometimes weeks. Meta gives no fixed time.')],
 [('/instagram-disabled-account-integrity-notice/','Instagram account integrity'),('/instagram-account-integrity-appeal-what-to-write/','What to write')],FBL+[CS])
notice('instagram-disabled-account-integrity-notice','ig','Instagram Disabled for “Account Integrity”: What It Means (2026)','Instagram account integrity',
 'Instagram disabled your account under account integrity? What the label means, what triggers it and the right appeal order. Unbanz: $800 upfront, 100% refund if it fails.',
 'Instagram disabled for account integrity.','What the notice means and the order to handle it in.',
 '<strong>On Instagram, “account integrity” usually points to inauthentic behaviour: automation or growth tools, bought followers, multiple accounts on one device, impersonation, or being linked to another account that was disabled.</strong> Appeal from the login notice, complete any video selfie only inside the official flow, and keep it short. If the appeal fails or says you can’t request another review, Unbanz handles Instagram cases for $800, paid upfront with a 100% refund if it fails.',
 [('Inauthentic behaviour','The usual meaning.'),('Video selfie','Official flow only.'),('Short appeal','Facts, not anger.')],
 [('triggers','Common triggers',ul(['Third-party growth, follow or DM automation apps.','Many accounts managed from one phone.','An account sold or transferred to you.','A linked account disabled for something else.'])),
  ('order','The order that works',ol(['Screenshot the notice and the date.','Remove third-party apps from your Meta account.','Appeal from the notice.','Complete identity checks only in the app.','Wait for the email; do not appeal again and again.']))],
 [('Will removing growth apps help?','It does not reverse the decision, but it avoids a second flag.'),('Is account integrity permanent?','After a rejected appeal it usually is, but cases are still reversed.')],
 [('/instagram-account-integrity-appeal-what-to-write/','What to write'),('/facebook-disabled-account-integrity-notice/','Facebook account integrity')],IGL+[CS])
